2-b32d-21348996e25b\n65:Conclusion: P4 made substantial algorithmic progress by implementing and testing a complex-valued, gauge-equivariant, Hermitian-attention Transformer prototype with physical channel simulation and coded-link evaluation. The strongest evidence is that signal symmetries and complex-valued operations were encoded directly into the model and some mechanisms showed reproducible value in controlled 1D ablations. However, the formal 2D result did not establish a learned-Transformer advantage; the largest 2D improvements came from better pilot/channel front-ends. The next decisive experiment is a strictly matched comparison where EM and classical receivers share the same physical front-end, pilot information, decoder, and inference budget, isolating only the learned module.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
